  "source": "Goldman Sachs",
  "title": "Americas Chemicals: OLN and HUN announce all-stock merger of equals creating a leading North American chemical company, OlinHuntsman",
  "type": "equity_research",
  "priority": "medium",
  "published": "2026-06-17",
  "insights": [
   "Olin Corp (OLN) and Huntsman Corp (HUN) announced a definitive agreement for an all-stock merger of equals to form 'OlinHuntsman', expected to close in 1H27.",
   "The deal targets $400mn+ in total synergies, including $300mn in cost/integration benefits and $100mn in raw material benefits by 2031.",
   "Pro forma 2025 sales are $12.5bn with $0.9bn EBITDA ($1.3bn including full synergies).",
   "HUN shareholders will receive 0.5476 shares of OLN for every 1 share of HUN, resulting in ~54.5% ownership for OLN shareholders and ~45.5% for HUN shareholders.",
   "HUN shares traded down 17% and OLN down 6% on the announcement, likely reflecting a correction after HUN's 30% outperformance since mid-March."
